IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcra-core`

-- Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 (Qld) -- from the seat of the INSURER: WorkCover Queensland, or
-- an employer licensed as a self-insurer (schedule 6, "insurer"), in its dealings with one claim.
--
-- The Act puts real deadline duties on the insurer: decide within 20 business days (s 134), tell the claimant why if it
-- has not (s 134(6)), start the basic weekly payment (s 146B), give the notice of assessment within 10 business days
-- (s 185), decide on a request to reassess within 10 business days (s 186(3)), refer to rehabilitation (s 220(3)). This
-- seat asks those questions as the insurer would ("By when must we ...?", "What must we pay ...?"). It is not a seat
-- for the Regulator: WorkCover and a self-insurer are parties to the claim, not officials deciding it from outside.
-- The rules are in wcra-core.l4; this module restates none and defines no name that wcra-seat.l4 defines.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 (Qld) -- the insurer's questions`

DECLARE `Insurer amount answer` IS ONE OF
    `we owe, in dollars` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `we owe nothing: past the first 5 years of the incapacity (ss 150-152, 144A)`
    `we owe nothing under part 11: a terminal latent onset injury already compensated (s 194(2))`
    `not covered: no deposited QOTE for that financial year (only 2026-27 is deposited)`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `QOTE for an earlier year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the insurer's QOTE for` `the day` `given` `QOTE for an earlier year` MEANS
    `the QOTE for the financial year containing` `the day` `given` `QOTE for an earlier year`

§§ `Deciding an application for compensation`

@export By when must we, as the insurer, decide this application for compensation (s 134(2): within 20 business days after it is made)?
GIVEN `the day the application was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the claimant made (lodged) the application with us
      `Queensland public holidays on weekdays in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Queensland public holidays fall on a Monday to Friday in the business days being counted (0 if none)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must we decide this application` IS
    `the deadline day` `the s 134(2) business days` `business days after` `the day the application was made` `with` `Queensland public holidays on weekdays in the period` `public holidays in between`

@export If we have not decided the application in 20 business days, by when must we tell the claimant our reasons and that it may seek a review (s 134(6))?
GIVEN `the day the application was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the claimant made (lodged) the application with us
      `Queensland public holidays on weekdays in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Queensland public holidays fall on a Monday to Friday in the business days being counted (0 if none)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must we tell the claimant why we have not decided` IS
    `the deadline day` (`the s 134(2) business days` PLUS `the s 134(6) business days`) `business days after` `the day the application was made` `with` `Queensland public holidays on weekdays in the period` `public holidays in between`

@export This application was lodged more than 6 months after the entitlement arose: must we, or may we, waive the time limit (s 131(1), (4)-(6))?
GIVEN `the day the claimant's injury was first assessed by a doctor` IS A DATE @desc The day a doctor (or nurse practitioner for a minor injury, or dentist for an oral injury) first assessed the injury: the entitlement arose that day (s 141(1))
      `the day the application was lodged` IS A DATE @desc The day the application was lodged with us
      `a medical assessment tribunal decided special medical circumstances exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a medical assessment tribunal has decided that special circumstances of a medical nature exist
      `it was lodged within 20 business days after incapacity was first assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether we are satisfied a doctor, nurse practitioner or dentist assessed the injury as resulting in total or partial incapacity, and the application was lodged within 20 business days after that first assessment
      `we are satisfied the delay was due to mistake, absence from Queensland or a reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether we are satisfied the claimant's failure to lodge in time was due to a mistake, absence from Queensland, or a reasonable cause
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
DECIDE `Must or may we waive the time limit` IS
    `the s 131 time limit answer` `the day the claimant's injury was first assessed by a doctor` `the day the application was lodged` `a medical assessment tribunal decided special medical circumstances exist` `it was lodged within 20 business days after incapacity was first assessed` `we are satisfied the delay was due to mistake, absence from Queensland or a reasonable cause`

@export If we allow this application, from what day are we liable for weekly compensation (ss 141(2), 131(2)-(3))?
GIVEN `the day the claimant's injury was first assessed by a doctor` IS A DATE @desc The day a doctor (or nurse practitioner for a minor injury, or dentist for an oral injury) first assessed the injury: the entitlement arose that day (s 141(1))
      `the day the application was lodged` IS A DATE @desc The day the application was lodged with us
      `the day the worker stopped work because of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker stopped work because of the injury
      `the day the worker was first assessed as unable to work` IS A DATE @desc The day a doctor, nurse practitioner or dentist first assessed the injury as resulting in total or partial incapacity for work
      `Queensland public holidays on weekdays in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Queensland public holidays fall on a Monday to Friday in the business days being counted (0 if none)
      `the injury resulted in death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether death is, or results from, the injury (s 131(2) then does not limit back-payment)
      `we have waived the back-payment limit under s 131(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether we have waived s 131(2) because the delay was due to mistake, absence from Queensland or a reasonable cause
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From what day are we liable for weekly compensation` IS
    `the first day the insurer is liable for weekly compensation` `the day the claimant's injury was first assessed by a doctor` `the day the application was lodged` `the day the worker stopped work because of the injury` `the day the worker was first assessed as unable to work` `Queensland public holidays on weekdays in the period` `the injury resulted in death` `we have waived the back-payment limit under s 131(6)`

@export We have allowed the application but do not yet have the information to work out the weekly payment: what basic weekly payment must we pay (s 146B(4)-(5))?
GIVEN `the week the payment is for` IS A DATE @desc Any day in the week the payment is for (it fixes the financial year's QOTE: 2026-27 is built in)
      `the QOTE for that financial year, if before July 2026` IS A NUMBER @desc If the day is before 1 July 2026: QOTE for that financial year in dollars, as notified by the Workers' Compensation Regulator; otherwise 0
      `the worker is engaged in full-time work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker is engaged in full-time work
      `the hours the worker usually worked a week in the preceding 4 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc If not full time: the hours the worker usually worked a week in the 4 weeks before (or a reasonable estimate)
      `the full-time hours a week for the position` IS A NUMBER @desc If not full time: the full-time hours a week for the worker's position (for example 38)
GIVETH AN `Insurer amount answer`
DECIDE `What basic weekly payment must we pay` IS
    CONSIDER `the insurer's QOTE for` `the week the payment is for` `given` `the QOTE for that financial year, if before July 2026`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered: no deposited QOTE for that financial year (only 2026-27 is deposited)`
    WHEN JUST `QOTE` THEN `we owe, in dollars` (`the s 146B basic weekly payment at` `QOTE` `full time` `the worker is engaged in full-time work` `hours` `the hours the worker usually worked a week in the preceding 4 weeks` `of` `the full-time hours a week for the position`)

@export By when must we start that basic weekly payment: the later of 5 business days after we allowed the application and the end of the excess period (s 146B(3))?
GIVEN `the day we decided to allow the application` IS A DATE @desc The day we made the decision to allow the worker's application
      `the day the excess period ends` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the excess period, during which the employer pays (s 65 and Regulation s 15: until weekly compensation paid exceeds the lesser of QOTE and the weekly payment)
      `Queensland public holidays on weekdays in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Queensland public holidays fall on a Monday to Friday in the business days being counted (0 if none)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must we start the basic weekly payment` IS
    IF DATE_SERIAL `the day the excess period ends` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the fifth business day`
    THEN `the day the excess period ends`
    ELSE `the fifth business day`
    WHERE
        `the fifth business day` MEANS `the deadline day` `the s 146B business days` `business days after` `the day we decided to allow the application` `with` `Queensland public holidays on weekdays in the period` `public holidays in between`

§§ `Paying weekly compensation`

@export What weekly compensation do we owe this totally incapacitated worker for the week (ss 147, 148, 150-155)?
GIVEN `the week the payment is for` IS A DATE @desc Any day in the week the payment is for (it fixes the financial year's QOTE: 2026-27 is built in)
      `the QOTE for that financial year, if before July 2026` IS A NUMBER @desc If the day is before 1 July 2026: QOTE for that financial year in dollars, as notified by the Workers' Compensation Regulator; otherwise 0
      `how the worker's employment is governed` IS AN `Employment basis` @desc One of: employment governed by an industrial instrument (s 150); employment not governed by an industrial instrument (s 151); a contract worker under s 152 (public service, government entity, university, electricity industry salaried, health service)
      `the worker's NWE` IS A NUMBER @desc The worker's normal weekly earnings, in dollars (s 106, Regulation ss 105-109)
      `the amount payable under the worker's industrial instrument or contract of service` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 107B amount (the weekly wage rate in the worker's usual employment, or an amount the Regulator approved) or the s 152 contract amount, in dollars; 0 if not under an instrument
      `the worker is casual or part-time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker was engaged in casual or part-time employment
      `the worker was on an age, disability support or class B widow pension when injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker was receiving one of those Commonwealth pensions when injured (s 154)
      `what the worker was earning when injured` IS A NUMBER @desc If s 154 applies: the worker's weekly earnings when injured, in dollars (0 otherwise)
      `what the worker may earn before the pension is reduced` IS A NUMBER @desc If s 154 applies: the weekly amount the worker may earn before the maximum pension is reduced, in dollars (0 otherwise)
      `the worker has demonstrated a DPI over 15% could result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker has demonstrated to us that the injury could result in a DPI of more than 15% (after the first 2 years)
      `the single pension rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum single disability support pension, as a weekly amount in dollars, without allowances
      `the week of the worker's incapacity` IS A NUMBER @desc Which week of the incapacity the payment is for (1 for the first week; weeks 1-26, 27-104, 105-260)
      `what the worker would have received from employment that week` IS A NUMBER @desc What the worker would have received from the employment that week if at work and not injured, in dollars (s 147)
      `the weekly amount we have decided to deduct under s 148` IS A NUMBER @desc The equivalent weekly amount of other payments or benefits we have decided to have regard to under s 148, in dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH AN `Insurer amount answer`
DECIDE `What weekly compensation do we owe` IS
    CONSIDER `the insurer's QOTE for` `the week the payment is for` `given` `the QOTE for that financial year, if before July 2026`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered: no deposited QOTE for that financial year (only 2026-27 is deposited)`
    WHEN JUST `QOTE` THEN
        CONSIDER `the weekly compensation for total incapacity for` (`Weekly facts` WITH
            `basis`                                                                      IS `how the worker's employment is governed`
            `NWE`                                                                        IS `the worker's NWE`
            `the amount payable under the industrial instrument or contract of service` IS `the amount payable under the worker's industrial instrument or contract of service`
            `engaged in casual or part-time employment`                                 IS `the worker is casual or part-time`
            `was receiving an age, disability support or class B widow pension when injured` IS `the worker was on an age, disability support or class B widow pension when injured`
            `the amount the worker was earning at the time of the injury`               IS `what the worker was earning when injured`
            `the amount the worker may earn before the maximum pension is reduced`      IS `what the worker may earn before the pension is reduced`
            `the worker has demonstrated to the insurer that the injury could result in a DPI of more than 15%` IS `the worker has demonstrated a DPI over 15% could result`
            `the single pension rate`                                                   IS `the single pension rate`
            `the week of the incapacity`                                                IS `the week of the worker's incapacity`
            `what the worker would have received from employment that week if not injured` IS `what the worker would have received from employment that week`
            `the weekly amount of other payments the insurer has decided to deduct under s 148` IS `the weekly amount we have decided to deduct under s 148`) `at` `QOTE`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `we owe nothing: past the first 5 years of the incapacity (ss 150-152, 144A)`
        WHEN JUST `the amount` THEN `we owe, in dollars` `the amount`

@export What is the most we may pay to redeem this worker's weekly payments (s 174: (156 x 70% of QOTE) less the weekly payments already paid)?
GIVEN `the day of the redemption` IS A DATE @desc The day of the redemption payment (it fixes the financial year's QOTE: 2026-27 is built in)
      `the QOTE for that financial year, if before July 2026` IS A NUMBER @desc If the day is before 1 July 2026: QOTE for that financial year in dollars, as notified by the Workers' Compensation Regulator; otherwise 0
      `the total weekly payments already paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the weekly payments already paid to the worker, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Insurer amount answer`
DECIDE `What is the most we may pay to redeem weekly payments` IS
    CONSIDER `the insurer's QOTE for` `the day of the redemption` `given` `the QOTE for that financial year, if before July 2026`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered: no deposited QOTE for that financial year (only 2026-27 is deposited)`
    WHEN JUST `QOTE` THEN `we owe, in dollars` (`the s 174 redemption cap at` `QOTE` `less` `the total weekly payments already paid`)

@export How much overpaid compensation may we recover from the worker, or deduct from later weekly payments (s 170)?
GIVEN `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount paid to the worker for the application, in dollars
      `the amount the worker was entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the worker was entitled to, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much overpaid compensation may we recover` IS
    `the overpayment recoverable under s 170` `the amount paid` `the amount the worker was entitled to`

-- Situation: the insurer has had the worker's injury assessed for permanent impairment.
§§ `Permanent impairment`

@export By when must we give the worker the notice of assessment, with any lump sum offer (s 185: within 10 business days after we receive the assessment)?
GIVEN `the day we received the assessment` IS A DATE @desc The day we received the report of the assessment of the worker's permanent impairment
      `Queensland public holidays on weekdays in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Queensland public holidays fall on a Monday to Friday in the business days being counted (0 if none)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must we give the notice of assessment` IS
    `the deadline day` `the s 185 business days` `business days after` `the day we received the assessment` `with` `Queensland public holidays on weekdays in the period` `public holidays in between`

@export What lump sum must we offer this worker for the DPI (ss 180, 181, 187 and Regulation s 117)?
GIVEN `the day we make the offer` IS A DATE @desc The day we make the offer: the lump sum is worked out as at that day (s 180(3))
      `the QOTE for that financial year, if before July 2026` IS A NUMBER @desc If the day is before 1 July 2026: QOTE for that financial year in dollars, as notified by the Workers' Compensation Regulator; otherwise 0
      `the worker's DPI` IS A NUMBER @desc The worker's degree of permanent impairment, in percent (10 for 10%)
      `the part of the DPI from earlier or non-compensable conditions` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of the DPI, in percent, attributable to a condition existing before the injury or one not compensable (0 if none)
      `the worker's earlier lump sum entitlement for the same part of the body` IS A NUMBER @desc Any earlier entitlement to lump sum compensation for an injury to the same part of the body (not industrial deafness), in dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH AN `Insurer amount answer`
DECIDE `What lump sum must we offer` IS
    CONSIDER `the insurer's QOTE for` `the day we make the offer` `given` `the QOTE for that financial year, if before July 2026`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered: no deposited QOTE for that financial year (only 2026-27 is deposited)`
    WHEN JUST `QOTE` THEN `we owe, in dollars` (`the s 180 lump sum at` `QOTE` `for a DPI of` `the worker's DPI` `less` `the part of the DPI from earlier or non-compensable conditions` `and` `the worker's earlier lump sum entitlement for the same part of the body`)

@export The worker disagrees with the DPI and asks to be assessed again by a different entity: by when must we decide whether to do so (s 186(3): within 10 business days)?
GIVEN `the day we received the worker's request` IS A DATE @desc The day we received the worker's request to have the injury assessed again
      `Queensland public holidays on weekdays in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Queensland public holidays fall on a Monday to Friday in the business days being counted (0 if none)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must we decide whether to have the injury assessed again` IS
    `the deadline day` `the s 186(3) business days` `business days after` `the day we received the worker's request` `with` `Queensland public holidays on weekdays in the period` `public holidays in between`

@export With the notice of assessment, must we also give the worker copies of ss 10, 237(3), 239, 240 and 316 and advise of the irrevocable election (s 189(2))?
GIVEN `the worker's DPI` IS A NUMBER @desc The worker's degree of permanent impairment, in percent (10 for 10%; 0 if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must we give the worker the election sections with the notice` IS
    `the worker's DPI` LESS THAN `the DPI threshold for the election`

§§ `Rehabilitation`

@export Must we refer this worker to our accredited rehabilitation and return to work program (s 220(3)-(4))?
GIVEN `the worker receives compensation and has asked to be referred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker is receiving compensation for the injury and has asked us to be referred to a rehabilitation and return to work program
      `the worker's compensation stopped under s 144A, 168 or 190(2) and the worker has not returned to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker stopped receiving compensation under s 144A, 168 or 190(2) and has not returned to work because of the injury
      `the worker already participates in our accredited program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker is already participating in our accredited rehabilitation and return to work program
      `we are satisfied the program cannot further assist the worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether we are satisfied the program is not able to further assist the worker with rehabilitation for the injury
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must we refer the worker to a rehabilitation program` IS
    `s 220(3) requires a referral` `the worker receives compensation and has asked to be referred` `the worker's compensation stopped under s 144A, 168 or 190(2) and the worker has not returned to work` `the worker already participates in our accredited program` `we are satisfied the program cannot further assist the worker`

@export May we suspend this worker's compensation, by written notice, because the worker has not taken part in rehabilitation (s 232(2))?
GIVEN `the worker failed or refused to participate in rehabilitation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker has failed or refused to satisfactorily participate in rehabilitation, including a return to work program or suitable duties we arranged
      `the worker had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker had a reasonable excuse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we suspend the worker's compensation for not taking part in rehabilitation` IS
    `the insurer may suspend compensation under s 232(2)` `the worker failed or refused to participate in rehabilitation` `the worker had a reasonable excuse`

-- Situation: a worker has died because of the injury.
§§ `Compensation on a worker's death`

@export A worker has died because of the injury: what lump sum compensation must we pay for the dependants, or to the estate (ss 194, 200, 201, 201A)?
GIVEN `the day of the worker's death` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker died (READING: it fixes the financial year's QOTE; 2026-27 is built in)
      `the QOTE for that financial year, if before July 2026` IS A NUMBER @desc If the day is before 1 July 2026: QOTE for that financial year in dollars, as notified by the Workers' Compensation Regulator; otherwise 0
      `a dependant was totally dependent on the worker's earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one dependant was, at the time of death, totally dependent on the worker's earnings
      `the worker left dependent members of the family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker left members of the family (s 28) wholly or partly dependent on the worker's earnings
      `the worker left a totally dependent spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker left a spouse (s 29) totally dependent on the worker's earnings
      `dependent members of the family under 6` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent members of the family are under 6
      `dependent members other than the spouse under 16 or students` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent members of the family other than the spouse (or totally dependent children of the spouse) are under 16, or under 21 and in full-time education (s 195)
      `the amount we consider reasonable for partial dependants` IS A NUMBER @desc If all dependants were partially dependent: the amount we consider reasonable and proportionate to their loss of dependence, in dollars
      `the worker left a spouse, issue or next of kin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there are no dependants: whether the worker left a spouse, issue or next of kin (Succession Act 1981)
      `the death is from a terminal latent onset injury already compensated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death is from a latent onset injury that is a terminal condition, for which the worker had received lump sum compensation or damages
GIVETH AN `Insurer amount answer`
DECIDE `What lump sum must we pay for the worker's death` IS
    CONSIDER `the insurer's QOTE for` `the day of the worker's death` `given` `the QOTE for that financial year, if before July 2026`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered: no deposited QOTE for that financial year (only 2026-27 is deposited)`
    WHEN JUST `QOTE` THEN
        CONSIDER `the lump sum on death for` (`Death facts` WITH
            `at least 1 dependant was totally dependent on the worker's earnings`        IS `a dependant was totally dependent on the worker's earnings`
            `the worker left dependent members of the family`                            IS `the worker left dependent members of the family`
            `the worker left a totally dependent spouse`                                 IS `the worker left a totally dependent spouse`
            `dependent members of the family under 6`                                    IS `dependent members of the family under 6`
            `dependent members, other than the spouse, under 16 or students`             IS `dependent members other than the spouse under 16 or students`
            `the amount the insurer considers reasonable for partial dependants`         IS `the amount we consider reasonable for partial dependants`
            `the worker left a spouse, issue or next of kin`                             IS `the worker left a spouse, issue or next of kin`
            `the death is from a terminal latent onset injury already compensated by a lump sum or damages` IS `the death is from a terminal latent onset injury already compensated`) `at` `QOTE`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `we owe nothing under part 11: a terminal latent onset injury already compensated (s 194(2))`
        WHEN JUST `the amount` THEN `we owe, in dollars` `the amount`
